{"term":"north","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:edab261e16b1736b3e","definition":"The direction towards the pole to the left-hand side of someone facing east, specifically 0°, or (on another celestial object) the direction towards the pole lying on the northern side of the invariable plane.","example":"Minnesota is in the north of the USA.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":["south"],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable, uncountable","wordFamily":["Norse"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/north#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:265dfc2f482335ad3e","definition":"The up or positive direction.","example":"Stock prices are heading back towards the north.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":["south"],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable, uncountable","wordFamily":["Norse"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/north#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:c5b9c7949caba01e8f","definition":"The positive or north pole of a magnet, which seeks the magnetic pole near Earth's geographic North Pole (which, for its magnetic properties, is a south pole).","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":["south"],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable, uncountable","wordFamily":["Norse"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/north#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:7a8f14d64f2ad879c8","definition":"Alternative letter-case form of North (“a northern region; the inhabitants thereof”).","example":"[…] and after independence the north clung to sugar production longer than the south, with the result that when the north took […]","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":["south"],"collocations":[],"usage":"alt-of",